course: dictionary
lesson: 12132
title: Words that praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how much someone deserves to be admired. Commendable is one of them, and it is a formal word. It means deserving praise, or worthy of being admired. «Her honesty was commendable, even when the truth was hard to say.» The sentence praises her honesty, so commendable must mean worth praising.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mia's drawing was not perfect, but her effort was commendable.» The drawing was not perfect, yet the writer still gives praise. So commendable can praise an action or a try, even when the result is not the best.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Her honesty was worthy of praise, even when the truth was hard to say» still makes sense, so you have it right. Teachers and speakers often use commendable this way, in phrases like commendable effort or commendable courage.
fact: Commendable means deserving praise, or worthy of being admired.
fact: «Commendable» is a formal word, so you will often see it in school reports and speeches.
fact: «Commendable effort» means the effort was good, even if the result was not perfect.
fact: Commendably is the adverb: «She handled the problem commendably» means she dealt with it in a praiseworthy way.
fact: Phrases to learn: commendable courage, highly commendable, commendable honesty.
exercise: «Her honesty was commendable, even when the truth was hard to say.» What does commendable mean here? | *Deserving praise | Very loud | Worth hiding | Hard to find
exercise: «The team lost the match, but their commendable effort made the crowd cheer.» What does commendable tell us about the effort? | Lazy and careless | *Good and worthy of praise | Secret | Too short to count
exercise: «Ben's commendable courage helped him climb the rope.» Find and copy the word that means worthy of praise. | *commendable | helped | courage | climb
test: The teacher wrote, «Your project is highly commendable.» What does highly commendable mean? | *Very worthy of praise | Very late | Very disappointing | Very small
test: «She handled the difficult question commendably.» What does commendably describe? | *In a praiseworthy way | In a sad way | In a hurry | In a noisy way
exam: Which phrase uses commendable to praise a try, even though the result was not perfect? | commendable puddle | commendable sandwich | *commendable effort | commendable shadow
